     "text": "Certainly! Below is a **Linear Regression class** implemented using **NumPy**, following the latest coding guidelines provided by your mentor, including the requirement to import the `pedantic` module at the beginning of code files.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 **LinearRegression Class Using NumPy**\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pedantic  # Required import as per mentor's guidelines\n\nclass LinearRegression:\n    def __init__(self, fit_intercept=True):\n        self.fit_intercept = fit_intercept\n        self.coefficients = None\n        self.intercept = None\n        self.X = None\n        self.y = None\n\n    def fit(self, X, y):\n        \"\"\"Fit the model to the training data.\"\"\"\n        if X.shape[1] == 1:\n            X = np.column_stack((np.ones(X.shape[0]), X))  # Add intercept term\n\n        self.X = X\n        self.y = y\n\n        # Ensure X and y are numpy arrays\n        self.X = np.array(self.X)\n        self.y = np.array(self.y)\n\n        # Compute the coefficients using normal equations\n        X_T = self.X.T\n        X_T_X = np.dot(X_T, self.X)\n        X_T_y = np.dot(X_T, self.y)\n\n        self.coefficients = np.linalg.solve(X_T_X, X_T_y)\n        self.intercept = self.coefficients[0] if self.fit_intercept else 0\n\n    def predict(self, X):\n        \"\"\"Predict values based on the fitted model.\"\"\"\n        if X.shape[1] == 1:\n            X = np.column_stack((np.ones(X.shape[0]), X))  # Add intercept term\n\n        self.X = np.array(X)\n        predictions = np.dot(self.X, self.coefficients) + self.intercept\n        return predictions\n\n    def score(self, X, y):\n        \"\"\"Compute the R\u00b2 score for the model.\"\"\"\n        y_pred = self.predict(X)\n        y_true = np.array(y)\n        y_pred = y_pred.reshape(-1, 1)\n        y_true = y_true.reshape(-1, 1)\n\n        # Compute mean squared error\n        mse = np.mean((y_true - y_pred) ** 2)\n        # Compute total sum of squares\n        tss = np.mean(